# One-click first run: the app installs the WinUSB binding itself (2026-10-31 00:30-00:47)

## what changed for the user
Before: unzip -> find setup\ -> run a .cmd -> read a page -> aim Zadig at MI_02 -> Replace
        Driver -> come back -> double-click DropBridge.exe.
Now:    unzip -> double-click DropBridge.exe -> one "yes" -> one UAC -> it starts receiving.
Zadig stays in setup\ as the fallback, not the primary path.

## how the application path works
RadioBinding (supervisor): WMI Win32_PnPEntity where DeviceID like the MI_02 instance;
Service == WinUSB means done. When it is not, Install() re-launches itself with
ShellExecute runas (one UAC), then in the elevated copy:
  certutil -addstore -f Root           dropbridge-driver.cer
  certutil -addstore -f TrustedPublisher dropbridge-driver.cer
  pnputil /add-driver airbridge-winusb.inf /install
and re-reads the service. Every step is appended to data\logs\driver-install.txt.
Tray menu gained 安装驱动（首次使用） for the case the prompt was dismissed.

## the driver package (built here, not downloaded)
packaging\driver\airbridge-winusb.inf   narrow WinUSB INF: one hardware id
                                        (USB\VID_0BDA&PID_C820&MI_02), winusb.sys
packaging\driver\airbridge-winusb.cat   catalog over the INF, 7,744 B
packaging\driver\dropbridge-driver.cer   self-signed code-signing cert, 794 B
tools\Build-DriverPackage.ps1           makecat + signtool (Windows SDK), no WDK/inf2cat
Built with cert thumbprint 349454D4A4BC3590A33755B46A22EAB4486C931D (RSA-2048, SHA-256,
15 years, private key stays in the build machine store and is not shipped).
signtool verify /pa: "Successfully verified", 0 errors (checked against the exported .cer
as a temporary trust anchor, removed afterwards).

## verified
exe --install-driver on this machine (already WinUSB): exit 0, log "already bound",
  and it did NOT call pnputil (idempotent, no driver churn).
same call from the extracted zip: exit 0, same log line.
exe --bogus: exit 2 and a supervisor.log line, instead of silently starting the tray.
zip -> tray run: registered HKCU Run -> the packaged exe path, wrote data\autostart-offered,
  balloon shown; the Run value was removed again after the test.
zip still checks out: --check exit 0, no MISSING.

## still unproven
The real unbound -> bound transition has NOT been exercised on this machine: doing it means
unbinding the only working dongle first. Recovery is known (re-run Zadig, or this installer),
but it needs a deliberate decision and a UAC click. Until then the driver install is
"built and signature-verified", not "on-air proven".
